Description: Fail PS extraction when the file cannot be read.
 When the file could not be opened, the PS extractor logged a warning and still reported
 success, without metadata. A file which vanished before it was extracted was then handled as
 a successful extraction, which is how the extractor reached the crash
 extractor-check-resource-before-printing.patch fixes. The error from g_file_read() is
 propagated instead, so that such files are handled as failed extractions.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/localsearch/-/merge_requests/707
Last-Update: 2026-11-01
